              fail; limiter 144 cases paid within 4 lines; isr_w / isr_x 240
              cases; negatives detected: forced 3.5 MHz exit, limiter removed
              (also -7.3 to -7.5% in JNext), R one off, isr_x R / interrupt
              lines / speed, 3 unit controls, rom3_left, the old tail; unit
              460 of 461 cases PASS (open: the guard object outside the figure
              table, unreachable in play, leaves its build out of the pace
              target)

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: the trophy screen after the title drawn
              clean, the walk-on scene, kick-off and the match reached, frames
              viewed; flicker 300 frames of the match: 0 out of step, 0
              vanished, 0 transients; 15-minute soak against the original
              .z80: no crash, both runs wait at the half-time menu (build from
              frame 24,900, original 25,850; the profile never presses ENTER
              there), which the soak calls a freeze in the build only because
              its score differs; beeper (port 0xFE) writes a second equal to
              the control's in all 30 pace trials (2,429 quiet, 2,336 busy and
              sound), 50 interrupts a second in both; the limiter removed
              reads -7.3 to -7.5% (caught); no person played it

  Coverage    first halves with the computer and player 1 on Kempston (random
              input); no second half, no 2-player game, no Match Day Special,
              no menu changes; no cheats (the archive's .pok has only value-
              asking entries); no loading screen (the tool adds its stub in
              the highest bank, and this build holds Sinclair's ROM in bank
              47)

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
